{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"AC4 RESCOPED -- change 2608 ABANDONED after operator rejection, and the rejection is correct.\n\nThe objection: 'This contaminates rebar documentation with local environment setup relevant only to a specific user.'\n\nThat is right, and I should have caught it when I wrote the brief. The detector reads\n~/.local/state/rebar-dev/ plus the reject-streak and current files written by this host's\nmain-tracking LaunchAgent. That updater is MACHINE-LOCAL -- it is documented in\ndocs/local-env-main-tracking.local.md, which is git-ignored precisely because it is one operator's\nsetup rather than rebar behaviour. Shipping a 'rebar doctor' scan for it, plus a docs/user-guide.md\nsection, puts that setup into the product and into documentation every user reads.\n\nWHAT I CONFLATED, and this is the useful distinction going forward:\n - A GENERAL capability: warn when the installed rebar is far behind main. That could affect any\n   developer with a stale pipx/uv install and is arguably worth having.\n - A SPECIFIC one: read THIS HOST'S updater state files to detect THIS HOST'S LaunchAgent stalling.\nThe change implemented the general shape on top of the specific paths, which is why it looked\nreasonable and was still wrong. Note the implementing agent had already removed an XDG_STATE_HOME\nread after the config-ownership gate objected -- the right instinct, applied one level too shallow.\n\nAC4 IS REPLACED BY:\n 4. A stalled main-tracking updater is detectable WITHOUT depending on the remote alert sink, by a\n    mechanism that lives OUTSIDE this repository's shipped surface -- e.g. in the machine-local\n    tooling alongside rebar-dev-update.sh, or in the LaunchAgent itself. It must add nothing to\n    rebar's CLI, its docs, or its public API. Verified by running it on this host and observing it\n    report the real state.\n 4b. If a GENERAL 'your installed build is N commits behind' capability is wanted in rebar proper,\n    that is a SEPARATE ticket and a separate change. It must reference no machine-local paths and no\n    LaunchAgent state, and must degrade to 'not applicable' wherever such state is absent. Do not\n    fold it back in here.\n\nSTATE OF THIS BUG: AC1 and AC2 are effectively resolved -- the updater had failed 122 consecutive\nruns and, after the patch was applied, published 6125c5345f01 with reject-streak back to 0. AC3 was\nwithdrawn by operator decision. AC5 (pruner 'Directory not empty' and the partial-release stub)\nremains open and untouched. So what is left here is AC4's replacement and AC5.\n\nNot closing: the remaining work is real, and closing on the strength of the half that landed would\noverstate it."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788516460187853001,"uuid":"80ed77ab-0c4a-4b5e-ab28-2f08713fb8b2"}